## 🗂 Project Structure

This project is intentionally shipped as **one self-contained file** for easy sharing and zero setup:

```
apex-autoworks/
└── index.html      # HTML structure + embedded CSS (<style>) + embedded JS (<script>)
```

Internally, `index.html` is organized into clearly commented sections:

```
<head>            → meta tags, Google Fonts, embedded CSS with design tokens
<body>
 ├─ <header>       → sticky nav / dashboard cluster
 ├─ #page-home     → hero, slider, categories, value props
 ├─ #page-cars     → toolbar (search/filter/sort) + car grid
 ├─ #page-details  → gallery + specs + EMI calculator
 ├─ #page-categories
 ├─ #page-favorites
 ├─ #page-booking  → test drive form
 ├─ #page-about
 ├─ #page-contact
 ├─ #page-login    → login/register/logout
 ├─ <footer>
 ├─ inquiry modal
 └─ <script>       → data, state, render functions, event handlers
```

Pages are implemented as toggled `<section class="page">` blocks (single-page-app style) — navigation swaps visibility via JavaScript instead of separate HTML files, so the whole site loads instantly with one request.

