## 🧠 How It Works

### Car data
All 24 cars live in a single JavaScript array (`CARS`) near the top of the `<script>` block:

```js
{id:1, brand:"Toyota", model:"Camry", type:"Sedan", fuel:"Petrol",
 trans:"Automatic", year:2024, price:32500, mileage:15, seats:5,
 color:"Pearl White", lock:101, desc:"..."}
```

Add, remove, or edit cars by editing this array — the grid, filters, slider, categories, and details page all render from it automatically.

### Images
Car photos are loaded live from **LoremFlickr** (`loremflickr.com`), keyed by body type (e.g. `sedan`, `suv`, `sportscar`, `electriccar`) plus a `lock` ID per car so each listing gets a stable, repeatable set of photos. This means:
- No image files to host or upload.
- Photos are real automotive photography, but **not the exact make/model pictured** (LoremFlickr matches by keyword, not by car).

To use your own photos instead, replace the `carImg()` / `carImgLarge()` functions with paths to local images (e.g. `/images/cars/toyota-camry-1.jpg`).

### Data persistence
Everything is stored in the browser's `localStorage` — no backend or database:

| Key | Stores |
|---|---|
| `apex_favorites` | Array of favorited car IDs |
| `apex_theme` | `"dark"` or `"light"` |
| `apex_users` | Registered demo accounts (username + password, plaintext — demo only) |
| `apex_current_user` | Currently logged-in user |
| `apex_bookings` | Submitted test-drive bookings |

⚠️ **Not production auth.** Passwords are stored in plain text in `localStorage` purely for demo/prototype purposes. Do not reuse this pattern for a real login system.

